<!--
    kuna decodehalt (DIV-151): a RETURN kuna planted because it could NOT
    decode the bytes says so, instead of printing as an ordinary `return;`.

    FlowInfo ends a path it cannot follow with an ARTIFICIAL HALT - a
    CPUI_RETURN carrying the constant 1 and one of the getHaltType() bits.
    Three of those bits are decode failures rather than program returns:
    badinstruction, unimplemented and missing.  Upstream PrintC::opReturn
    (printc.cc:774) renders them as the pseudo-calls halt_baddata() /
    halt_unimplemented() / halt_missing(), and processInstruction buffers
    "Bad instruction - Truncating control flow here" at the failing address
    plus a header warning on the function.  kuna ported the halt but neither
    the rendering nor the warnings, so a function that ran off into bytes it
    could not read ended with a bare `return;` and nothing said so.

    Stage model: P2 lift / flow-classification.

    dh_fn (0x100000): test edi,edi / je +1 / ret / .byte 0x06
      0x06 (PUSH ES) is not an instruction in 64-bit mode, so the je target
      at 0x100005 is undecodable and the flow follower halts there.

    `option voidtailreturn on` is set because that is what `kuna decompile`
    runs (mode auto -> aggressive), and it is the seam this rendering has to
    survive: voidtailreturn elides a void function's trailing bare `return;`,
    and the artificial halt has exactly that shape, so without the halt-type
    exclusion in elidable_void_tail_return the truncation marker is deleted
    and its warning lands on whatever statement decoded before it.

    The body ends halt_baddata() carrying the truncation warning (assert #2)
    under a prototype carrying the header warning (assert #3); assert #1 pins
    the silent form - a clean early exit under a prototype that says nothing -
    to zero occurrences.
-->
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x100000" readonly="true">
85ff7401c306
</bytechunk>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x100000" name="dh_fn"/>
</binaryimage>
<script>
  <com>parse line extern void dh_fn(int x);</com>
  <com>option voidtailreturn on</com>
  <com>lo fu dh_fn</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>quit</com>
</script>
<stringmatch name="DECODEHALT #1: the undecodable path never reads as a clean early exit under a silent prototype" min="0" max="0">^void dh_fn\(int4 x\)$
^\{$
^  if \(x\)$
^    return;$
^\}$</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="DECODEHALT #2: the halt names the decode failure and carries the truncation warning" min="1" max="1">^  halt_baddata\(\); // warn: Bad instruction - Truncating control flow here$</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="DECODEHALT #3: the function header says the body is incomplete" min="1" max="1">^void dh_fn\(int4 x\) // warn: Control flow encountered bad instruction data$</stringmatch>
